   "notes": "Standard third-order Birch-Murnaghan pressure-volume EOS in the Eulerian finite-strain convention at room temperature. V0, K0, and K0_prime were all fitted in EosFit7c; none was fixed or adopted. Parenthesized coefficient errors are stored as printed, but the article gives no confidence level or covariance matrix. Table 2 also prints a BM3 re-fit to Vanpeteghem et al. (2003): V0=211.41(11) A^3, K0=155(5) GPa, K0_prime=6.7(5). That comparison reduction belongs to the older powder dataset and is not a second parameterization of the 2018 single-crystal observations. The fitted V0 is a zero-pressure extrapolation because the only ambient observation was intentionally omitted. The experimental pressure envelope is not a phase-stability guarantee."
  },
